649
00:46:46,880 --> 00:46:50,720
And we don't always see clearly how that's going to work out or what that's going to look like.

650
00:46:50,720 --> 00:46:52,940
But you were faithful the first time.

651
00:46:52,940 --> 00:46:56,920
And so we can trust you to be faithful the second time.

652
00:46:57,860 --> 00:47:03,980
I pray this morning that each and every person in this room will find encouragement and hope,

653
00:47:03,980 --> 00:47:06,140
knowing that you're going to return.

654
00:47:06,140 --> 00:47:08,100
You're going to wipe away every tear from our eyes.

655
00:47:08,100 --> 00:47:10,480
You're going to take away the weapons of war.

656
00:47:10,480 --> 00:47:15,780
You're going to set up a kingdom of peace and justice among the land forever.

657
00:47:15,780 --> 00:47:19,220
Nothing can take that away from us.

658
00:47:19,220 --> 00:47:23,400
So in the meantime, God, we look towards you with hope.

659
00:47:24,020 --> 00:47:30,320
And we live lives that proclaim the message of Jesus to the lost, the broken, the hurting, the poor, the powerless.

660
00:47:30,320 --> 00:47:32,940
We preach that message until you come back.

661
00:47:32,940 --> 00:47:38,100
God, encourage our hearts this morning to continue to live for you.

662
00:47:38,100 --> 00:47:41,020
We love you so much.

663
00:47:41,020 --> 00:47:41,880
We thank you for Jesus.

664
00:47:41,880 --> 00:47:43,480
It's in his name we pray.

665
00:47:43,480 --> 00:47:49,900
Church, thanks for hanging with me through a college lesson on end times.

666
00:47:49,900 --> 00:47:52,080
I hope you guys have a great rest of your day.

667
00:47:54,020 --> 00:48:24,000
We'll be right back.
